Upstream-Name: myna
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/canonical/myna/issues
Source: https://github.com/canonical/myna
Comment:
 /usr/lib/myna-whisper bundles the Python distributions resolved from the
 upstream server/uv.lock (faster-whisper, CTranslate2, PyAV with its FFmpeg
 libraries, NumPy, tokenizers, huggingface-hub...), installed from PyPI
 wheels at build time. Each one, with its licence, is listed in
 /usr/share/doc/myna-whisper/PYTHON-DEPENDENCIES, and its own licence files
 are kept in its *.dist-info directory under /usr/lib/myna-whisper. The PyAV
 wheel also carries FFmpeg (LGPL-2.1-or-later) and GMP (LGPL-3.0-or-later)
 shared libraries in av.libs/; NumPy carries OpenBLAS (BSD-3-Clause).
 All are compatible with AGPL-3.0-or-later.
 Third-party material in the upstream tree is listed in the upstream NOTICE
 file, installed as /usr/share/doc/myna-whisper/NOTICE. Model weights are not
 shipped: myna-whisper-fetch-model downloads them (MIT) from Hugging Face.

